how to hire remote workers successfully  and my business have had a mix of hiring  people remotely and people who also work  you know out of my office and I recently  had to go through the process again of  hiring somebody new remotely as we're  growing and I wanted to share my  experience with you because a lot of  people get this wrong a lot of  entrepreneurs make mistakes here and end  up losing tons of time in the process so  here's the first thing I do it's it's  really important I'll write out  everything that I want the person  understand okay I want them to know what  my company stands for what we're all  what we're all about right helping  entrepreneurs believing in entrepreneurs  I will write what their job entails all  the different tasks that they have to do  and it'll be one big fat messy ugly  paragraph so Evan you're so mean why  would you do that why don't you make it  easy for them to get the information I  don't want it to be easy you know as  part of the job requirement is being  able to work through hard stuff right I  try to make it as easy as possible once  I've hired them I don't want their lives  to be hard but but I need them to be  detail-oriented and see who's a worker  who's not right it's an attitude  somebody will see that huge Peregrine's  I don't want to read that great I don't  want you as part of my company I want  somebody who's gonna take the time to  read it if you start seeing stuff about  believing entrepreneurs and it doesn't  inspire you to keep going if you're not  hungry enough to work for me then I  don't want you as part of my team it's  perfect they've self eliminated  themselves the next thing I'll do is  right in the middle of that ugly nasty  long terrible paragraph I'll ask two  questions one will be how many Twitter  followers do I have and I'll say please  share this as your first sentence in  your response back to me and then I'll  ask them what do you like about  entrepreneurs because if you don't like  entrepreneurs you're not gonna have a  great time working for me so the first  one tests did they actually read that  long paragraph and the second one will  test why do they want this job because  you're not just looking for a bum in a  chair you're looking for someone who's  gonna give you their heart and soul  because they love what you're all about  so I posted the job I got hundreds of  requests  80% of them 80% of them didn't even  mention the Twitter thing that I posted  that means they just saw the ad saw was  a marketing position and they sent in  their cover letter in their resume 80% I  would have burned my time reading all of  their profiles their resumes or cover  letters wasting my time when they spent  five seconds looking at the job at  that's what's gonna happen if somebody  does not say in their first cent is like  I clearly asked how many Twitter  followers do I have then I don't read  their profile it saves me a ton of time  see this is what you need to do this is  why hiring it can be so painful and  frustrating because you bring it on the  wrong people and spending time with the  wrong people  okay so 80% gone I just cut my work down  by a lot next the next 10% wrote  something like I don't know how many  Twitter followers you have because you  didn't give me your account how hard is  it to find Evan Carmichael on Twitter  that was it was a small simple stupid  easy test so all you showed me now is  that you read then read the whole  paragraph but you have zero  resourcefulness to go out and find how  many Twitter followers I have you type  Evan Carmichael Twitter you'll find me  it's not that hard  so those 10% are gone too I don't want  them in my business if I have to explain  every single thing step by step and you  have zero resourcefulness then you're  not gonna be a good fit at my company  and they shouldn't be a good fit at your  company either you should care about  this stuff this is important the last  10% of the ones who actually said how  many Twitter followers I had that's like  baseline right I've already eliminated  90 percent of people who were just  wasting my time who didn't even care  about this those last 10 percent then I  look at what their response was not just  the Twitter followers but how did they  answer the second question why are they  like entrepreneurs do they do they have  it in their blood was a part of their  family what is it and you can tell some  people speak with passion they speak  from the heart I don't care for this job  if they're perfect English or not I'm  not asking to be a writer but I want to  feel something from from their response  they're not just saying I love  entrepreneurs and I hope to be one  someday  that's not what I want so you get down  to like the last two or three percent of  people and then I'll hire them on a  small job a trial job this is something  that they would do for me and I give  them a limit so I'll say you have 10  hours to do this job and I'll give them  like four tasks to do and some people  will take the full ten hours to do it  and some people will will not get it  done within the ten hours and some  people do anything I'll just claim the  ten hours and and so you're losing a  little bit of money on these people but  what you want to see is how long does it  take somebody to do the task  I give them something that is hard and I  see  can they get this done within that ten  hour limit  are they being honest with me if they  finish early are they billing me for ten  hours are they gonna bill me for the 8.5  that they work that's who I want I want  the hustler the one who said I got all  this stuff done and I did it under time  what's up that's who I want to hire so  you can do a lot of the work of  screening people upfront you build the  crazy long paragraph you ask them a  question that is relatively easy to find  if they just read what you wrote you  give them something that relates to what  you're all about something passionate  and see what the response is  and the people who write back and give  them some kind of trial job to test  their skills is test if they're the  right fit for you or not small amount of  money up front but it's worth it for  getting the right person anyway that's  my process it's worked its work  repeatedly I hope you'll use it to make  better hiring decisions I don't want you  to be the entrepreneur who tries to hire  somebody it doesn't work out and you say  this is not for me I can't hire people  I'm gonna do it myself because that's  not how you have a real impact in the  world you've got to bring people on and  it's tough and it's harder you make  mistakes and the first person you hire  is probably gonna not gonna last with  you right it just happens but I want you  to minimize your mistakes and I want you  to believe that the hiring people can  work and you can you can bring on people  to really help you build something  powerful so that's how I do it believe  you guys liked this video please give it  a thumbs up below I'd love to hear what  you have to think you have a question  about my process you want to learn more  leave it below you have another question  about your business in general leave it  below in the  let me give you the response thank you  guys so much and I'll see you soon
 

